  "reply_raw": "The recurring pattern is consistent: incident-purpose reads of file-hr-comp with an open ticket throughout. The safety-critical invariants are purpose=incident and ticket_open=1; classification and ttl varied across tasks (0/1 and 15/60) but were admitted either way, so they're not gating. A standing rule should encode the security-relevant conditions and cap TTL, not hardcode the variable fields.\n\n{\"mode\": \"precedent\", \"rule\": {\"action\": \"read_restricted_file\", \"resource\": \"file-hr-comp\", \"conditions\": {\"purpose\": [\"eq\", \"incident\"], \"ticket_open\": [\"eq\", \"1\"], \"ttl_min\": [\"le\", \"60\"]}}}",
